A||||6||rogergarrison||PittsburgH Vintage Gran Prix||||1||
Z||000000||rogergarrison||07-20-2001||06:18 AM||||All you Pittsburgh guy going to the show tommorro...Ill be coming up I-79 from Wheeling. Whats the easiest directions to get to the park?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mark||07-20-2001||08:58 AM||||Roger,<P>I 79 north to Exit 15 (Pittsburgh exit?).  You wll be pick up Rt 22-30 (aka Penn Lincoln Parkway) to Pittsburgh.  Pass thru Fort Pitt Tunnel (be ready for a stunning view of Pittsburgh when you exit the tunnel).  Cross Fort Pitt Bridge in the RIGHT LANE and BEAR RIGHT (continuation of Rt 22-30).  Continue about 1 or 1.5 miles to FORBES AVE (it may also be called OAKLAND) off ramp (right lane again).  Follow Forbes ave. to Schenley Park.  <P>Here's a schedule for the Western PA Fiero Club indicating where they will meet..http://members.nbci.com/wpfc/2001events.html<P>Have fun!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||kslish||07-20-2001||03:10 PM||||Hey Roger,<P>When do you plan on arriving?  The West Penn Fiero Club is planning on meeting at the old Isaly's building parking lot in Oakland at 8:30a.m. to motorcade as a group to the showfield around 9:00a.m.  If you want directions, I can probably get them (I know where it is, but don't know the exact address off the top of my head).  <P>Mark's directions are great, only thing I will add is that is once you are on Forbes Ave you will enter Oakland (aka the University of Pgh. campus).  There should be signs for Schenley Park eventually on your right.  To get to the park from Forbes, look for Pitts Hillman Library on the right (It's before the Carnegie Library and Museum...if you pass the Carnegie, you've gone too far), and make a right there (should be a Schenley Park sign right at that corner).  Follow the old cars (should be a lot of them) across the bridge to Schenley Park/Phipps Conservatory.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-20-2001||03:20 PM||||i wont leave here till prob 8 or 8:30 so Ill get there probably around 10 am. (depending on Hiway Patrol along the way   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">...)<P>Ill ask em where the Fieros are when I get there.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||07-20-2001||04:32 PM||||Roger,<P>As Ken said, Schenley Park is a right turn past Hillman Library.  However, parking will likely be scarce and the road is blocked off for the event.  You may be able to find a parking spot somewhere around the Cathedral of Learning (very tall stone Gothic building - you can't miss it) and just walk over to the park.  Just follow all the people!||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||07-20-2001||08:45 PM||||I plan on showing my car. My car NEVER EVER sits in a parking lot. Did you need to be preregistered or something. If I cant show, let me know cause I wont be coming.||||reg||1
Z||000006||kslish||07-20-2001||10:08 PM||||No preregistration is needed (heck, I'm not even preregistered).  You can register at the gate.  I hardly ever preregister for local shows since stuff can come up at the last minute to prevent me from going and then I'm out the cash.<P>The bridge will be open.  Once you drive over the bridge, there will probably be some cops (to tell non-show cars to turn around) and some race officials.  Just ask one of them where the entrance to the showfield is (Schenley Park will be on your left as soon as you cross the bridge).<P>Look forward to seeing you tomorrow Roger...<P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||1
